    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 green). `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured address form across the stack so it fully satisfies the spec while keeping the flat `address` backward-compatible.\n\n**API contract** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)\n- Added `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` to `OwnerFields` (both optional in the schema; validated at runtime). These are inherited by the `Owner` response schema, so the normalized values are echoed back.\n- Removed `address` from the required list so a structured-only owner passes Bean Validation; `address` is documented as the composed response value.\n\n**Domain** (`model/Owner.java`)\n- Added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` fields (columns `address_line1` / `address_line2`) with getters/setters. MapStruct auto-maps them in both directions.\n\n**Controller** (`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`)\n- `normalizeAddress` now normalizes `addressLine1`, `addressLine2` and the flat `address` (reusing `AddressNormalizer`). When `addressLine1` is non-blank the structured fields are preferred and the flat `address` is composed as `addressLine1` + (`\" \" + addressLine2` when present); otherwise the flat address keeps its own normalized value.\n- `addRequiredAddress` now accepts an owner supplying an address in *either* form (non-blank `addressLine1` **or** flat `address`) plus city, reporting `address` only when both are absent/blank.\n\n**Schema** (`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`)\n- Added nullable `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns to the `owners` table (the test suite runs on the in-memory hsqldb profile).\n\nThe household hash, postcode validation and locality read `city`/`postcode`, which are supplied identically in both forms, so those derivations are unchanged; only the stored/returned `address` string is now the composed structured value when structured fields are present.",
